   "evidence": "`grep -n dimVector_eq_zero code/TauCeti` returns only the new one-directional lemma; the file's only other vanishing lemma is `dimVector_zero` at DimensionVector.lean:66, about `(0 : QuiverRep k Q)`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Quiver/Representation/DimensionVector.lean",
   "fix": "State the characteristic form `dimVector_eq_zero_iff : (\u2200 i, FiniteDimensional k (M.obj ((Paths.of Q).obj i))) \u2192 (dimVector M = 0 \u2194 IsZero M)`, or add the missing `IsZero.dimVector_eq_zero` (which needs no finite-dimensionality hypothesis) alongside it.",
   "issue": "`isZero_of_dimVector_eq_zero` gives only one direction. For a general `IsZero M` the converse `dimVector M = 0` is not stated anywhere; `dimVector_zero` (line 66) covers only the literal `0` object, so a consumer must route through `dimVector_eq_of_iso (h.iso (isZero_zero _))`.",
